+/* AWE32Emu: optional MFBEN loopback.
+ *
+ * A real AWE32 has the MFBEN jumper (MIDI FeedBack ENable), which brings the
+ * data written to the MPU-401 back to its own input. That lets the resident
+ * AWEUTIL /EM catch the MIDI a game sends to the MPU and play it on the
+ * EMU8000. 86Box does not emulate that path - the write goes straight to the
+ * host MIDI - so the MIDI emulation in the guest has nothing to listen to.
+ *
